Incoming Gradient

dout

Shape:

(batch_size, output_channels, output_height, output_width)

Meaning:

gradient wrt convolution output

or:

“How much did each output activation
 affect final loss?”

⸻

Why dx Has Input Shape

dx.shape
=
self.x.shape

because backward output shape must equal forward input shape.

This invariant exists for every layer.

⸻

Why dW Exists

dW

stores:

gradient wrt filters

This tells:

how filters should change

⸻

Critical CNN Insight

Same filter was reused everywhere spatially.

So:

all spatial usages contribute
into same filter gradients

This is:

parameter sharing

⸻

The Most Important Line

dW[f] += region * grad

Meaning:

this local image region
contributed to output error

So corresponding filter weights receive blame.

⸻

Why += ?

Because:

* filter reused everywhere
* many spatial positions contribute
* gradients accumulate

⸻

Input Gradient

dx_padded += self.weights[f] * grad

This redistributes blame backward into:

the earlier feature maps

Important:

We are NOT reconstructing images.

We are propagating:

sensitivities / blame signals

⸻

Deep Backprop Insight

Forward pass propagates:

information

Backward pass propagates:

responsibility

